answer.text:
The current sensitivity of a moving coil galvanometer can be increased by (any one):
1. increasing the number of turns in the coil ($I_s\propto N$);
2. increasing the magnetic field strength ($I_s\propto B$);
3. using a material of smaller torsional constant $\left(I_s\propto\dfrac{1}{k}\right)$;
4. increasing the area of cross-section of the coil.
